-- Robscript Team - My Little Pony Card Opening
-- Game: My Little Pony Card Opening | placeId 76275796126573
-- Window: RightControl | Unload: Settings -> Unload | API: getgenv().RobScriptTS
--
-- What it does:
--   Packs      - a rotation of up to four sets: opens the chosen number of packs of the first set, then the
--                same for the next one and around again. Packs are bought from the shop when the stash is
--                empty and there are enough coins for it.
--   Duplicates - after every open it sells duplicates above the keep limit, protected by the rarity tier,
--                favourites, shelf copies and display copies.
--   Pony Pairs - plays the memory table: deals a board, asks the server for one card at a time and matches
--                the pairs it has already seen.
--
-- How it works: the game is one client LocalScript that talks to ReplicatedStorage.Remotes. The hub calls the
-- very same remotes - BuyPack(set, qty), OpenPack(set, fast, packs, sides), SellCards({id = count}) and
-- Memory("deal" / "flip", index). Nothing is hooked or rewritten, every request is the call the game itself
-- makes, only without the pack animation in front of it.

do
	local existing = getgenv().RobScriptTS
	if type(existing) == "table" and type(existing.Destroy) == "function" then
		pcall(existing.Destroy)
	end
end

